scenario.en:
A getter looks like a pure query but mutates on each call:<br/><pre><code>class Counter {
  private n = 0;
  get current(): number { return ++this.n; }
}
const c = new Counter();
console.log(c.current);
console.log(c.current);</code></pre>What does each <code>console.log</code> print, and why is this a command/query separation bug rather than just surprising?

